Work, for beside thee he standeth
to bless;
He will direct thee thro’ earth’s
wilderness;
God will protect thee, no foes shall
oppress;
Work for Him, then, while you may.

Tell the world, the whole wide world;
Bear the news from shore to shore;
Tell the whole wide world of Jesus,
Praise His name for ever more!

Thus I would go on missions of
mercy,
Following Christ from day unto day;
Cheering the faint, and raising the
fallen;
Pointing the lost to Jesus the way.

For "they that wait upon the Lord
shall renew their strength,
they shall mount up with wings,
they shall mount up with wings as
eagles:
They shall run and not be weary;
they shall walk and not faint;
They shall run and not be weary;
they shall walk and not faint;
They shall run and not be weary-,
shall walk and not faint.”

Dismiss me not from thy service, Lord,
But train me for thy will;
For even I, in field so broad,
Some duties may fulfil;
And I will ask for no reward.
Except to serve thee still.

Our Master all the work hath done
He asks of us today;
Sharing his service, every one
Share too his sonship may:
Lord, I would serve and be a son;
Dismiss me not, I pray.

Send the Light the Lord commands
it;
To His Holy Word attend:
“Go ye forth and preach My gospel;
Lo! I’m with you to the end.”

Set my soul afire, Lord, in my daily life,
Far too long I’ve wandered in this
day of strife;
Nothing else will matter but to live
for Thee,
I will be a  witness, for Christ lives in me.

It pays to serve Jesus whatever
may betide.
It pays to be true whate’er you may
do;
Tis riches of mercy in Him to abide;
it pays to serve Jesus each day.

A charge to keep I have, God to glorify,
A never dying soul to save, And fit it
for the sky. ,

To serve the present age, My calling to fulfill;
O may it all my pow'rs engage To
do my Masters will!

Any where with Jesus I can safely go;
Anywhere He leads me in this world
below;
Anywhere without Him dearest joys
would fade;
Anywhere with Jesus I am not afraid.

Give of Thy sons to bear the
message glorious;
Give of thy wealth to speed them on
their way;
Pour out thy soul for them in pray’r
victorious;
And all thou spendest Jesus will
repay.

Millions now in sin and shame are
dying.
Listen to their sad and bitter cry;
Hasten, brother, hasten to the
rescue;
Quickly answer, “Master, here am I"

Speed thy servants, Saviour, speed them;
Thou art Lord of winds and waves:
They were bound, but Thou hast
freed them;
Now they go to free the slaves.
Be Thou with them, Be Thou with
them;
'Tis Thine arm alone that saves.

Vet blest that end in woe.
And those sad days;
Only man’s blame below;
Above God’s praise.

Often I’m hindered on my way.
Burdened so heavy I almost fall;
Then I hear Jesus sweetly say;
“Heaven will surely be worth it all.”

There dwells my Lord, my King,
Judged here unfit to live;
There angels to Him sing,
And lowly homage give;

Thro' time’s ever changing seasons,
I am pressing t’ward the goaJ;
‘Tis my heart's sweet native
country,
Tis the homeland of my soul;
Many lov’d ones, cloth’d with
beauty,
In those wondrous glories share;
When I rise, redeemed, forgiven,
I shall be no stranger there.

There for ever and for ever
Alleluia is out-poured;
For unending, for unbroken
Is the feast-day of the Lord;
All is pure and all is holy
That within thy walls is stored.

Sleep on, beloved, sleep and take thy rest;
Lay down thy head upon thy
Saviour's Breast;
We love thee well, but Jesus loves
thee best;
Good night, good night, good night!

There is no grief in heaven;
For life is one glad day;
And tears are of those former
things
Which all have pass’d away.

When I stand before the throne,
Dress'd in beauty not my own;
When I see Thee as Thou art,
Love Thee with unsinning heart;
Then, Lord, shall I fully know,
Not till then, how much I owe.

When you start for the land of heavenly rest,
Keep close to Jesus all 'he way;
For He is the Guide, and He knows
the way best;
Keep close to Jesus all the way.

It is glory just to walk with Him,
It is glory just to walk with Him;
He will guide my steps aright
Thru the vale and o'er the height;
It's glory just to walk with Him.

I shall see my Saviour’s face,
When I get home;
Sing again of saving grace,
When I get home;
I shall stand before Him;
Gladly I’ll adore Him;
Ever to be with Him,
When I get home.

We speak of the land of the Blest.
Of that country so bright so fair;
And oft are its glories confessed;
But what must it be to be there?
